            <ArticleTitle>Does bupivacaine irrigation of third molar sockets reduce postoperative pain? A double blind controlled trial.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>96-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A double blind controlled randomised trial suggested that irrigation of third molar sockets with bupivacaine 0.75% produces significant reduction in pain scored on the first post-operative morning (p less than 0.01). However, this technique produces no significant reduction in opiate or oral analgesic consumption.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
